{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746645778352832545","content":"Most of the feed back was positive. The negative points mainly came from players who felt that they had a lack of player agency when we had to make corrections. From a top down perspective my reaction to the issues I watched as well as player feed back can be found in the new server rules. I won't post direct text here from any particular player, because that feels somewhat inappropriate. There were some complaints of favoritism and nepotism, as well as long wait times during combat. As well as some hard feeling from a couple of the players who we had to call out. Some of this is us, which is one of the reasons I asked for so many dms for next year. DM burn out is a real thing in roanoke. But some of it was also players failing to take personal responsibility for their attitudes and actions. We didn't ask anyone to leave this year when maybe we should have. It's always been my goal to try and retain people with kindness.","created_at":"2020-08-28T04:56:40.433000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"748767990757195867","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
