{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746645778352832545","content":"Some of the way the infighting happened comes down to bad game design on our part. Some of it comes down the way cliques treat each other as just part of the human condition.  And some of it comes down to how intensely players attach to their characters in our format.","created_at":"2020-08-28T05:00:37.008000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-28T05:13:39.713000Z","id":"748768983024402442","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746645778352832545","content":"What went wrong is something I've thought about often, some of my character flaws involve being blunt and wanting to fix things as soon as I perceive there to be a danger, or a situation that could end up hurting others. But on the other side of that coin, I find my self analyzing my self for faults when the folks who are doing the negative things sometimes do not.  Try to remember that though we are running a public server this is also a free service. We are volunteers giving our time in a labor of love. When that labor is met with petty squabbles, bitterness and resentment it can be tough to stay humble and keep serving. People can sometimes find themselves caught in despair or attitudes of entitlement and forget that the events happen daily because we are playing a game that tells a complete story. Sometimes they forget that this isn't a single player experience and that their characters reactions are also a player choice. And sometimes we need to remember that people are concerned about their reputation. Which is a valid concern. We are weighing between likely consequences of taking steps to intervene and the consequences of our inaction in a case by case string of choices.","created_at":"2020-08-28T05:11:05.308000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-28T05:29:42.513000Z","id":"748771618305605714","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746645778352832545","content":"Shenanigans day and the cult of castor really set a rift between people. The bipartisanship of the cliques became an echo chamber of folks taking sides and wanting to protect their friends. Offense is a stumbling block that isn't easily overcome. There were a handful of people who swung too hard either into feeling the guilt of their decisions or into feeling defensive and assuming no guilt whatsoever. That is something we can't control. All we can do is do our best regardless of unexpected fall out.","created_at":"2020-08-28T05:38:51.024000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-28T05:39:14.529000Z","id":"748778604825018469","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
