{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"746645778352832545","content":"so i may have thought of the first task I wouldn't mind getting mods involved in.  I would like a document with lore created from the epilogues.  Not the story, but the facts that would impact world lore.  Some examples could be:\n\n-Roanoke Chinn are literally raised on stories, not only of gil, but the town as a whole, since their spawning pool is in the town itself, which might make them a bit more distinct from other chinn schools.\n\n-Some of the plants Leaf planted on both sides of the ocean started sprouting sandiberries after his funeral\n\n-within a few decades roanoke has a very large goblin tribe.\n\nsome of this stuff might never come up, but it could be handy to kind of have a digest of lore the players created.  I have read all the epilogues (well I'm about half way through webs) but I cant keep all the factual details in mind, and a digest might be cool when we are working on world lore.\n\nI also would like to suggest that the players for viola and lucky create a larger racial breakdown of jackalopes, as they had investment in the race, and likely created some of the lore on the fly.  I could also post up my chinn one, not only so they see what I'm talking about, but also so i can get input on making it better.  I still think that players should take some agency that departs from those descriptions, but having a bit more of a blurb might encourage people to play the homebrew races a bit more.","created_at":"2020-08-29T11:55:26.279000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"749235764058914827","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
