{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"746645778352832545","content":"Basic concept I am building on for how to work lairs and vehicles is to think of \"squares\" as a resource. This will of course be a number of squares the footprint of the structure occupies but also can be used to describe how many squares a balloon or a lifter or whatnot can lift and also translate to \"squares\" of movement and the like. Not sure if we want a Catan style combine specific resources to buy upgrades or if we want to just use gold for that? We could also require specific amounts of gold, silver, platinum if we wanted to be able to limit building more than we limit other purchasing power. If we have a setting reason for needing platinum to build vehicles for example we make platinum more prized and have a unique utility to it.","created_at":"2020-08-30T17:33:42.934000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"749683282266030110","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
